
P15
=======

Problem : Product Discount Eligibility Based on Age and Purchase History
Problem Statement:

You are tasked with assigning a discount code to customers based on their age and purchase history. The rules are as follows:

If the customer is under 18 years old, they are eligible for a "TeenDiscount".

If the customer is between 18 and 60 years old, they are eligible for a "RegularDiscount".

If the customer is above 60 years old, they are eligible for a "SeniorDiscount".

If the customer has made more than 5 purchases, they are eligible for a "LoyalCustomerDiscount".

If the customer is under 18 and has made more than 10 purchases, they get an additional "YoungLoyaltyBonus".

Input Example:

Age: 25

Number of Purchases: 6

Output Example:

DiscountCode = ["RegularDiscount", "LoyalCustomerDiscount"]



Solution:

#discounts = new java.util.ArrayList(),

// Get the age and number of purchases
#age = #this.get("age") != null ? #this.get("age").toString().toInteger() : 0,
#purchases = #this.get("purchaseCount") != null ? #this.get("purchaseCount").toString().toInteger() : 0,

// Assign discounts based on age
#discounts.add(#age < 18 ? "TeenDiscount" : 
               (#age <= 60 ? "RegularDiscount" : "SeniorDiscount")),

// Assign loyalty discounts based on purchase count
#discounts.add(#purchases > 5 ? "LoyalCustomerDiscount" : ""),

// Add Young Loyalty Bonus if under 18 and more than 10 purchases
#discounts.add(#age < 18 && #purchases > 10 ? "YoungLoyaltyBonus" : ""),

new org.sourceid.saml20.adapter.attribute.AttributeValue(#discounts.toString().replace("[", "").replace("]", "").replace(",", ""))
